  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The full test suite passes (1909 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nThe fix is one line in `src/click/core.py`. A child context now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)` instead of inheriting the parent's whole map. A subcommand called `sub` therefore reads its defaults from `default_map[\"sub\"]`.\n\nI added three tests to `tests/test_defaults.py`:\n- **Subcommand lookup:** `sub` picks up its value from the map, and a subcommand missing from the map falls back to the option's own default.\n- **Nested groups:** `cli grp sub` reads from `{\"grp\": {\"sub\": {...}}}`.\n- **Group option plus subcommand:** a group-level option from the top-level key still works next to a subcommand's nested entry.\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry. I can add one if you want it.",
